    "description": "The ILRS contribution to ITRF2020-u2025 consists of a pair of time series of weekly station position estimates, together with daily Earth Rotation Parameters (ERPs), namely X-pole, Y-pole, and excess Length-of-Day (LOD), estimated over 7-day arcs covering the period 2021.0\u20132026.0 and aligned with calendar weeks (Sunday to Saturday). In total, two different data sets are provided, which can be identified by the <sol type> in the filename. The <pos+eop> files comprise station position estimates and ERPs and are obtained by combining loosely constrained weekly solutions submitted by each of the eight official ILRS Analysis Centers. The resulting combined solution is also loosely constrained. In contrast, the <eop> solutions are minimum-constrained and contain ERPs only. Both the individual Analysis Center solutions and the combined solutions follow strict standards agreed upon within the ILRS Analysis Standing Committee (ASC) to provide ITRS products of the highest possible quality. NOTE: The <yymmdd> in the filenames refers to the last day of the respective week. Until September 2022, the combined solutions are based on observations of the four geodetic satellites LAGEOS-1, LAGEOS-2, Etalon-1, and Etalon-2. From September 2022 onwards, observations of LARES-2 are additionally included in the combined solutions. The secondary combination solution was provided by the Goddard Earth Sciences Technology and Research II\u00a0/Goddard Space Flight Center (GESTAR II/GSFC) Greenbelt, Maryland, USA.",
